            <div xml:id="d727">

                <pb facs="0740" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10790: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-05-09T17:00:00+03:00">May 9, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>136. For Secretary and Under Secretary. It would appear that although suggestion
                    reported my 111, April 26, was made as a result of intimation from King Greek
                    Government ultimately rejected it. It is also understood that that Government
                    took great offence on learning of Turkish approach to Germans (my 117, April 30)
                    of which it had not been informed in advance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
